REPAIRAGENT-OCI THOUGHTS: [0m The issue is consistent with cgroup v2 controller propagation: memory.max in the container cgroup only becomes active when the memory controller is enabled in the parent cgroup's cgroup.subtree_control. The current cgroupfs path enables controllers for the target path, which makes controllers available to children of the container cgroup but can leave the container itself without memory controller files/limits, exposing max. A focused low-risk fix is to enable controllers on the parent cgroup before creating/entering the target cgroup, while retaining the existing target enable for nested cgroups. I will apply this in cgroup-cgroupfs.c with explanatory comments and validate via the supplied build.
